THE CORE WHY
The tax pack computed agent fees inline as weeks x weekly_rent x
management_fee_pct, which can only reproduce a recurring percentage. Measured
against the agent's own FY2026 annual summary for OWN10905, the actual total was
$2,851.20 (management $1,573.00 + lease fees $1,210.00 + lease preparation
$33.00 + bank & sundries $35.20) while the estimate produces roughly $1,728.57 —
and it over-counts weeks while doing so, assuming 31.4 tenancy weeks when rent
covered 26.

Mirrors lib/tax/rental-income.ts on purpose: actual preferred, estimate as a
labelled fallback, both carried so the caller can show the cross-check.

DESIGN DECISIONS
- Commission and sundries are returned SEPARATELY. Management, letting and lease
  fees feed the ATO "Property agent fees and commission" line; bank and admin
  charges feed "Sundry rental expenses". Keeping them apart is what leaves the
  commission figure directly comparable to the estimate it replaces.
- The estimate has NO sundry component and returns 0 for it. A percentage of
  rent cannot produce a bank charge, and inventing one would be fabrication.
- Null return, never 0, when nothing is known. Zero would assert the agent
  charged nothing, which nothing in the data supports.
- A null individual fee IS treated as zero: statement #7 genuinely charged no
  letting or lease fee. Absent statement vs absent line item are different
  things.
- Exclusive week span, matching accruedRentForFy, so a full year is 52 weeks
  rather than 52.14.

THE `partial` FLAG — the non-obvious part
When only SOME payments in the year have confirmed fees, the actual is genuine
but incomplete. In the real FY2026 case it resolves to $1,619.20 from statements
#1 and #7, which is SMALLER than the $1,728.57 estimate and well under the true
$2,851.20 across all seven. Preferring the actual silently would understate the
deduction with no indication why — the opposite of the problem this track set
out to fix. `partial`, `paymentsInYear` and `paymentsWithConfirmedFees` exist so
Phase 5 can disclose it as a pack omission instead of hiding it.

This was not in the approved plan. It emerged from having real data: with all
seven statements the flag would never fire, and the gap would have shipped
invisible.

